    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d849">

                <pb facs="0968" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg824"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5166</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-03">July 3, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received August
                        2.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2174</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Legation’s despatch
                    No. 1832, of December 31, 1928,<anchor n="87" xml:id="d849-f1"/> respecting the
                    service of the Hukuang Railways Loan of 1911, I have the honor to state that a
                    partial default occurred on the payment by the Chinese Government of the service
                    of the loan due on June 3rd. This matter was brought to the attention of the
                    Legation, in the customary manner, in a letter of June 17th from Mr. Charles R.
                    Bennett, American Group Representative in Peking of the Hukuang Railways Loan
                    Group Banks, a copy of which is enclosed.<anchor n="87" xml:id="d849-f2"/>
                    Likewise enclosed is a copy of the joint note of protest of June 24th, addressed
                    by the Diplomatic Representatives of France, the United States of America, and
                    Great Britain, to the Minister for Foreign Affairs,<anchor n="87"
                        xml:id="d849-f3"/> on this subject.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clarence B.
                            Hewes</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">First Secretary of
                        Legation</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
